le.warn("Unable to save navigation scroll state",a)}}, 56, 40)</script></header><div class="font-sans"><main class="grow"><script id="page-metadata" type="application/json">{"title":"GPT Image 2.5 | OpenAI's Flare and Sunburst Image Models on fal","description":"GPT Image 2.5 is OpenAI's image model on fal, in two variants: Flare for everyday generation at 50% lower latency than GPT Image 2, and Sunburst for intricate detail. Generate and edit at up to 3840px, with transparent backgrounds and six quality levels. Available now via API.","openGraph":{"title":"GPT Image 2.5 | OpenAI's Flare and Sunburst Image Models on fal","description":"OpenAI's GPT Image 2.5 is live on fal in four endpoints: Flare and Sunburst, each with text to image and editing. Half the latency of GPT Image 2, up to 3840px, and six quality levels from under half a cent an image.","type":"website","url":"https://fal.ai/gpt-image-2.5","images":["https://ir7z8qsacw4tk54b.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/gpt-image-2.5/v2/og.jpg"]},"twitter":{"card":"summary_large_image","title":"GPT Image 2.5 | OpenAI's Flare and Sunburst Image Models on fal","description":"GPT Image 2.5 is on fal. Flare for everyday generation, Sunburst for intricate detail, both with precise editing. Up to 3840px and transparent backgrounds.","images":["https://ir7z8qsacw4tk54b.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/gpt-image-2.5/v2/og.jpg"]},"alternates":{"canonical":"https://fal.ai/gpt-image-2.5"}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://fal.ai/#organization","name":"fal","alternateName":["fal.ai","Fal","fal-ai"],"legalName":"Features & Labels Inc.","url":"https://fal.ai/","description":"fal is the generative media inference platform: call 1,000+ image, video, audio and 3D models through one API, or deploy your own models on serverless GPUs.","knowsAbout":["Generative media","AI inference","Serverless GPUs","Model deployment","Image generation models","Video generation models","Audio generation models"],"logo":"https://fal.ai/apple-touch-icon.png","image":"https://fal.ai/og-thumbnail.webp","sameAs":["https://discord.gg/fal-ai","https://github.com/fal-ai","https://www.reddit.com/r/fal/","https://twitter.com/fal","https://www.linkedin.com/company/features-and-labels/","https://www.youtube.com/@Fal.AI.Official","https://www.instagram.com/madeonfal","https://www.tiktok.com/@madeonfal"],"email":"support@fal.ai","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"San Francisco","addressRegion":"CA","addressCountry":"USA","postalCode":"94105"}},{"@type":"WebPage","name":"GPT Image 2.5: OpenAI's Flare and Sunburst Image Models on fal","description":"GPT Image 2.5 is OpenAI's image model on fal, in two variants: Flare for everyday generation at 50% lower latency than GPT Image 2, and Sunburst for intricate detail. Generate and edit at up to 3840px, with transparent backgrounds and six quality levels. Available now via API.","url":"https://fal.ai/gpt-image-2.5","dateModified":"2026-09-08","provider":{"@id":"https://fal.ai/#organization"}},{"@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"GPT Image 2.5","applicationCategory":"MultimediaApplication","operatingSystem":"Web","description":"GPT Image 2.5 is OpenAI's image model on fal, in two variants. Flare is the default for most applications, with fast, high-quality generation and support for complex layouts. Sunburst is precision-focused for premium visual work, trading longer generation for extra fidelity on intricate detail. Each has a text-to-image and an editing endpoint, with output up to 3840px, six quality levels, transparent backgrounds, up to 16 reference images per edit and up to four images per request.","offers":{"@type":"Offer","price":"0.0041","priceCurrency":"USD","description":"Pay per image, from $0.0041 at low quality to $0.1002 for 4K at high quality, with editing slightly higher; billed by token with no subscription"},"provider":{"@id":"https://fal.ai/#organization"}},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is GPT Image 2.5?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"GPT Image 2.5 is OpenAI's image model, available on fal in two variants. Flare is the default for most applications, with fast, high-quality generation, natural lighting and support for complex layouts. Sunburst is the precision-focused variant, built for premium visual work, spending longer on a request in exchange for extra fidelity on intricate detail. Each variant has a text-to-image endpoint and an editing endpoint, four in total."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between Flare and Sunburst?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"They are two tunings of the same model with an identical API. Flare is the everyday choice and returns faster. Sunburst spends longer and holds finer detail, which matters when the image will be viewed large or cropped into. On the editing side, Flare changes only what is asked while keeping subject, composition and background intact, and Sunburst offers the tightest control across many rounds of revision. Pricing is the same for both, so the choice is about detail and generation time rather than cost."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does GPT Image 2.5 cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Cost depends on the size, the quality setting and whether you are generating or editing. Generating at the default high quality, a 1024 x 768 image is $0.0362, Full HD is $0.0395 and 4K is $0.1002. Dropping to medium takes those to $0.0091, $0.0096 and $0.0260, and low quality starts at $0.0041. Editing the same sizes costs a little more, because the reference image is billed as image input: $0.0445, $0.0478 and $0.1084 at high quality, and $0.0124 upward at low. Those edit figures assume one 1024 x 1024 reference, which adds about $0.008 on its own; a 3840 x 2160 reference adds about $0.012, and passing several references adds more again. Flare and Sunburst are priced identically, so choosing between them never costs anything. Underneath, the model bills by token: text at $5.00 per million input, and images at $8.00 per million input and $30.00 per million output, with cached input cheaper, and the total rounded up to $0.0001. There is no charge for text output."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What resolutions does GPT Image 2.5 support?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Presets cover square, portrait and landscape at 4:3 and 16:9, and 'auto' lets the model pick. You can also pass an explicit width and height: both edges must be multiples of 16, the long edge caps at 3840px, the aspect ratio at 3:1, and the total pixel count must fall between 655,360 and 8,294,400. That puts 4K at 3840 x 2160 within reach."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the quality settings?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Six: auto, low, medium, high, xhigh and max. The default is high. Higher settings increase detail, latency and token usage, so quality is the main lever on what a request costs. This is a step up from GPT Image 2, which topped out at high."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can it generate transparent backgrounds?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Set background to 'transparent' and choose PNG or WebP output, and the image comes back with a real alpha channel, ready to composite. JPEG has no alpha channel, so pair transparency with PNG or WebP."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does image editing work?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The edit endpoints take a prompt plus up to 16 reference images, and an optional mask URL when the change should be confined to a region. Feed one round's output back in as the next round's input to revise iteratively: the subject and composition carry through while each instruction changes one thing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is new in GPT Image 2.5?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"OpenAI's launch notes give Flare higher image quality than GPT Image 2 at 50% lower latency, along with sharper detail, more natural lighting and richer textures. Style adherence is stronger from one generation to the next, subjects from reference photos are better preserved, and editing instructions are followed more reliably across multiple turns, with earlier edits more likely to carry through. Complex layouts and transparent backgrounds are handled better. On the API surface, quality gains two levels above the old ceiling, xhigh and max."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does GPT Image 2.5 compare to GPT Image 2?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"GPT Image 2.5 adds two quality levels above the old ceiling, xhigh and max, and splits into two variants so a request can be pointed at speed or at detail. Both generations remain available on fal, and GPT Image 2 keeps its own page and endpoints at https://fal.ai/gpt-image-2."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use GPT Image 2.5 for commercial projects?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Images generated through the fal API can be used in commercial projects. Check fal's terms of service at https://fal.ai/legal/terms-of-service for full details on usage rights and licensing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I get started with the API?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Install the fal SDK for Python or JavaScript, grab an API key from your dashboard at https://fal.ai/dashboard/keys, and make your first request in a few lines of code. Serverless, with no GPUs to manage. The API documentation lists every parameter."}}]}]}</script><div class="bg-white text-landing-ink" style="--landing-accent:#115EF3;--landing-accent-soft:#C5E9FF;--landing-fill:#C5E9FF;--landing-glow:#99EDFF;--landing-surface:#F4F4F4;--landing-border:#D9D9D9;--landing-ink:#000000;--landing-sparkle:#ADFF00;--landing-outline:#96AFAC"><section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-white"><div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0"><div><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="398" height="364" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="absolute top-[144px] right-0 hidden 2xl:block" style="color:transparent" srcSet="/landing/v2/_decor/blue/hero-blob-right.svg 1x, /landing/v2/_decor/blue/hero-blob-right.svg 2x" src="/landing/v2/_decor/blue/hero-blob-right.svg"/><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="236" height="338" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="absolute top-[163px] right-[397px] hidden 2xl:block" style="color:transparent" srcSet="/landing/v2/_decor/blue/hero-cluster-right.svg 1x, /landing/v2/_decor/blue/hero-cluster-right.svg 2x" src="/landing/v2/_decor/blue/hero-cluster-right.svg"/><img alt="" loading="lazy" width="354" height="128" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="absolute top-[-30px] left-[50px] hidden lg:block" style="color:transparent" srcSet="/landing/v2/_decor/blue/hero-cluster-left.svg 1x, /landing/v2/_decor/blue/hero-cluster-left.svg 2x" src="/landing/v2/_decor/blue/hero-cluster-left.svg"/></div></div><div class="relative mx-auto w-full max-w-[1376px] px-4 pt-16 pb-16 md:px-8 md:pt-24 md:pb-24 xl:pt-28 2xl:px-0"><div class="mx-auto flex max-w-[760px] flex-col items-center text-center"><span class="inline-flex w-fit items-center border rounded-[5px] bg-transparent px-[7px] py-1.5 md:px-3 md:py-2.5 border-landing-accent text-landing-accent font-heading font-medium text-landing-sm md:text-landing-title">New from OpenAI, live on fal</span><h1 class="mt-5 max-w-[820px] font-heading text-landing-display-m leading-[0.95] font-medium text-landing-ink md:mt-6 md:text-heading-6xl md:leading-none xl:text-[5rem]">GPT Image 2.5</h1><p class="mt-4 max-w-[640px] font-hal text-landing-body-m text-landing-ink md:text-landing-body">OpenAI&#x27;s GPT Image 2.5 is live on fal in two variants. Flare is the default for most work, at higher quality than GPT Image 2 with half the latency. Sunburst spends longer to hold intricate detail. Both generate from text and edit existing images, at up to 3840px.</p><div class="mt-7 flex w-full max-w-[680px] flex-col gap-2 rounded-2xl border border-landing-border bg-white p-2 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:rounded-full sm:pl-5"><label for="gpt-image-2.5-prompt" class="sr-only">Describe your image</label><input id="gpt-image-2.5-prompt" type="text" placeholder="Describe your image" class="min-w-0 flex-1 bg-transparent px-3 py-2 font-hal text-landing-body text-landing-ink placeholder:text-landing-ink/40 focus:outline-hidden" value=""/><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap border font-heading font-medium text-landing-title leading-[0.86] px-[26px] py-[17px] focus-ring transition-[background-color,border-color,color] duration-160 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-60 bg-landing-accent text-white border-landing-accent hover:opacity-90 shrink-0 rounded-full" href="/models/openai/gpt-image-2.5/flare/text-to-image?utm_source=landing&amp;utm_campaign=gpt-image-2.5&amp;utm_content=hero">Generate</a></div><div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2"><button type="button" class="focus-ring rounded-xs"><span class="inline-flex w-fit items-center border rounded-xs bg-white px-[11px] py-[3px] border-landing-accent text-landing-accent font-hal text-landing-sm transition-colors hover:bg-landing-accent-soft">A SaaS dashboard with legible stat tiles and a labelled chart</span></button><button type="button" class="focus-ring rounded-xs"><span class="inline-flex w-fit items-center border rounded-xs bg-white px-[11px] py-[3px] border-landing-accent text-landing-accent font-hal text-landing-sm transition-colors hover:bg-landing-accent-soft">A transit map with legible station names and a legend</span></button><button type="button" class="focus-ring rounded-xs"><span class="inline-flex w-fit items-center border rounded-xs bg-white px-[11px] py-[3px] border-landing-accent text-landing-accent font-hal text-landing-sm transition-colors hover:bg-landing-accent-soft">A candid studio portrait on 85mm at f/2</span></button><button type="button" c